      "summaryMarkdown": "PERF-1 data and coverage are complete and correct, but the findings prose contradicts the tables in places, so the document fails review until four small wording repairs land. The document records machine (Apple M5, 24 GB, macOS 26.6.2, matching meta.json), Chromium 147.0.7727.15 headed (raw JSON `browser`, `run.mjs headless: false`), commit 58257fe (all three scratch worktrees at HEAD 58257fe; wt-a diff = devtools feature in benchmark/Cargo.toml, wt-c diff = `AtomicBool::new(true)` in Window::new, matching the patches; wt-b clean), and the exact commands (identical to run-baseline.sh / log headers), with `--hold-clocks 3`, `--configs on`, retention/text/scroll on macos and web-webgpu. Tables equal compare.py's output; 50 cells spot-checked against medians of the raw JSON all match; the dropped (a) table-stream r1 is real (32 reports). CPU, GPU (macOS), `Window::draw` p50/p95, latency p50/p95, allocations, bytes, heap and footprint are all reported. No throwaway change is in this worktree (only the doc and AgentX state are modified).",
