      "deltaSummaryMarkdown": "Inspected the repaired `crates/gpui/tests/accesskit_025.rs`. `node_with_every_property()` now also sets `keyboard_shortcut`, `invalid`, `placeholder`, `orientation`, `level`, `row_index`, `column_index`, `row_count` and `column_count`, which covers every node setter in `crates/gpui/src/elements/div.rs`. The clone test checks each of them with a getter, and adds getter checks for `min_numeric_value` and `numeric_value_step`. `labelled_by` stays, with a comment tying it to the relations s03 resolves. The clear-and-set test now clears and sets again `disabled` (a flag) and `invalid` (an enum, set to a different variant), checking each state, and it also moves `bounds`. The product source is unchanged. The accesskit_025 check passed again at the new snapshot (4 tests). The unit and macOS checks were reused, which is valid because their inputs do not include the test file.",
      "reattestedFrom": "402f9bfa6bb43df151f1c4299047fa59bd40215caed5e23abf8884a09abe4130",
      "summaryMarkdown": "Everything else in AK-1 holds. The workspace pins `accesskit` 0.25.1 with `enumn`, `accesskit_consumer` 0.39.1, `accesskit_macos` 0.27.1, `accesskit_windows` 0.35.1 and `accesskit_unix` 0.24.0. `Cargo.lock` holds a single version of `accesskit` and of each adapter. No `accesskit::Tree` use remains in `crates/`. Both tree updates go through `a11y::tree_info()`, which sets toolkit name `gpux` and the crate version. The TreeInfo test would fail if `Tree::new` came back, and the order-independent equality test includes a negative case. The recorded checks passed (4 accesskit_025 tests, 13 `window::a11y` unit tests, macOS and Linux builds). AK-2 is met by the import checklist bullet, `docs/upstream/accesskit-0.25.md` and the provenance entry. The one minor finding is that the clone and clear-and-set tests do not cover all the properties gpux writes and clears. Not blocking: this sprint changed manifest dependencies, and the packaging rule asks for `cargo package --workspace`; the epic constraints already require it at the end of the epic.",
